## Native failure and limits of the evidence

Native run: https://github.com/saidi19/lumi-model/actions/runs/34805106054

Its checkout, executable/source pins, portable contracts and accepted-software
acquisition passed. Supervisor reports `process_failed`; the closed harness
report says `source_admission / fixture_failed`. The receipt verifier correctly
rejects the attempt as `qualification_rejected`.

This is a coarse stage, not an exact diagnosis. It spans source/bundle and helper
loading, subreaper setup, temporary-parent setup and the free-disk check. Generic
exceptions are also mapped to `fixture_failed`. A source-hash mismatch, import
error or disk shortage has not been established. Under the hash-bound code path,
image copying, Docker image loading/export, extraction and both guardian stages
were not reached.

Verified cleanup is limited to the outer harness being reaped with no adopted
children, and retirement of this acquisition's input archive and its parent.
No TERM/KILL or guardian/process-group signal was attempted. The failed receipt
does not prove whole-harness private cleanup, guardian cleanup, source
immutability or whole-job teardown.

## Evidence closure and resource accounting

The exact 1,981-byte aggregate ZIP matched its published SHA-256. Only its four
closed receipts were retained, totaling 3,048 bytes. Two sequential zero-network
receipt-verification passes completed on Python 3.11.15 and 3.13.7; all 146 prior
bindings and 78 source-admission bindings matched. Their success means failure
evidence is structurally valid, not that the qualification passed.

One earlier local checker attempt was stopped by its audit hook during stdlib
`ctypes` initialization. The checker setup was corrected before the two completed
passes; no published code or remote attempt was retried. The structural checker
is not comprehensive filesystem or whole-CI telemetry. Source/Spark's synthetic
forward/optimizer and dependency-download counters were not measured.

Prepublication used 8 of 8 metadata GETs. Post-run retrieval/metadata used 13 of
16 allowed GETs. Accepted software acquisition used its four responses once.
No raw job log, model/dataset payload, S3 or GPU request was made in the bounded
native/retrieval workflow. The configured 96 aggregate runner-minute ceiling is
not a billing estimate.

A prior approval-service credit error prevented a Source metadata request from
starting. After the user resumed, the same bounded read-only request passed the
ordinary approval path; no workaround was used.

